msgid "Check if the DTEP can act as a top level DTEP. This means that the document can be of this type. Some pseudo DTEPs cannot act as a top level DTEP, like <i>PHP</i> as they are always included as part of another DTEP, while some others can be included and act as standalone as well, like the case of <i>CSS</i>."
msgstr "Maak dit an, wenn sik de DTEP as DTEP op böverst Evene bruken lett. Dit bedüüdt, dat dat Dokment vun dissen Typ wesen kann. En poor Pseudo-DTEPs laat sik nich op de böverst Evene bruken, as t.B. <i>PHP</i>, wiel se jümmers binnen en anner DTEP stahn mööt, man en poor anner laat sik ok alleen bruken, as t.B. <i>CSS</i>."

